Test of label + text/ascii/type340 on the same line

// Verify that a location label and a text directive can appear on the same
// line.  Before the labelTrailer grammar fix this was a syntax error; the
// only workarounds were to split onto two lines or use a semicolon
// (e.g. msg,; text "hi").
//
// Three constructs tested:
//   msgtbl,  text  "Hi\n"       -- TEXT token (flexo-encoded)
//   dattbl,  ascii "AB"         -- ASCII STRING (two-token form)
//   gfxtbl,  type340 "XY"       -- TYPE340 T340STRING
//
// Each labeled block ends with a 013 stop-word.
// The final case confirms the ordinary label+instruction form still works.

100/

// Labeled text on the same line:
msgtbl, text "Hi\n"
        013

// Labeled ascii on the same line:
dattbl, ascii "AB"
        013

// Labeled type340 on the same line:
gfxtbl, type340 "XY"
        013

// Ordinary label + instruction on same line (must still work):
entry,  jmp entry

stop
